<title>UK: Fannie Mae ups 10-year bond to A$1.0 bln.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae ups 10-year bond to A$1.0 bln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and SBC Warburg, has been increased to A$1.0 billion from A$750 million.</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p> BORROWER   FEDERAL NATIONAL MORTGAGE ASSOCIATION</p>
<p> AMT	  A$1.0 BLN COUPON     **	  MATURITY    15.AUG.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    15.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/GB/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NP	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED FRIDAY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
